    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nA very fine Butterly brick fronted detached family home, one of four, tucked away off Highfield Road and to the rear of Oaklands Crescent. The spacious accommodation extends to approximately 290 sqm (3,121 sqft) comprising: welcoming reception hall off which there is a large living room with 15ft, ceiling and mezzanine level. A fully fitted and well-equipped Kitchen/Dining with gas range and integrated appliances. Off the kitchen there is a utility room and guest wc. A generous family/sitting room to the front completes the ground floor accommodation. \n\nA stairs from the hall provides access down to the basement level with home Gym, Games/Entertainment room with bar, guest wc and understairs store.\n\nUpstairs, on the first floor there are three bedrooms (main ensuite) and the main bathroom. On the second floor there is an attic room with shower off.\n\nOutside, to the front there is a low maintenance gravelled garden with off-street parking and wide side access. To the rear, a low maintenance paved and lawned garden with block build garden store.\n\nSuperbly located, off Highfield Road and close to Rathgar Village with its array of shops, cafes and restaurants, the beautiful Dodder walks, proximity to Milltown Golf Club (which is less than a mile door to door), being so close to the city centre and having Dartry Health Club and Brookfield Tennis Club and Palmerston Park a few minutes' walk away are only some of the attractions and benefits of this prime location. Excellent junior and senior schools are also close by, together with the LUAS at Cowper Road and Richmond Avenue South. Rathmines, Ranelagh and Terenure offer additional shopping, dining and leisure facilities close to your doorstep too."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nGround Floor - \n\n\nReception Hall: - \nWith oak flooring, decorative ceiling coving, and a glazed door leading to the main living area.\n\nLiving Room: - \nWith oak flooring, 15ft high ceiling, two Velux roof lights, coal effect gas fire, and a mezzanine level. Door opens to the rear garden.\n\nKitchen/Dining Room: - \nFully fitted with an extensive range of oak wall and floor units, marble worktops, 1½ bowl sink, integrated fridge/freezer, Britannia six-ring gas range with extractor above, integrated dishwasher, central island unit, display cabinet, window seat, tiled flooring, and door to rear garden.\n\nUtility Room & Guest WC: - \nIncludes pedestal wash hand basin, wc, plumbing for washing machine, gas boiler, storage, and oak timber flooring.\n\nFamily / Sitting Room: - \nwith cast iron fireplace and oak flooring.\n\nBasement Level - \n\n\nHome Gym: - \nFeaturing exposed brick fireplace and tiled flooring.\n\nGames/Entertainment Area: - \nWith exposed brick walls, tiled floor, Bar with sink.\n\nGuest wc: - \nIncludes wash hand basin and storage press.\n\nUnderstairs storage: - \nwith central vacuum system.\n\nFirst Floor - \n\n\nBedroom 1 (Rear): - \nWith pine timber flooring and fitted wardrobes.\n\nEn-Suite - \nincludes wc, wash hand basin, Jacuzzi-style shower, and pine flooring.\n\nBedroom 2 (Front): - \nWith fitted wardrobes and pine flooring.\n\nBedroom 3 (Front): - \nWith fitted wardrobe and pine flooring. Access to Jack-and-Jill bathroom.\n\nBathroom: - \nIncludes wash hand basin with mirror above, wc, Victorian-style freestanding bath, heated towel rail, timber panelled walls, and polished timber flooring.\n\nSecond Floor / Attic - \n\n\nAttic Room: - \nWith roof light, oak flooring, and under-eaves storage.\n\nShower: - \nWith wc, pedestal wash hand basin, power shower, tiled walls and floors, and Velux roof light.\n\n"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "<ul><li>Spacious family home of approx. 290sqm (3,121 sqft)</li><li>Gas Fired Central Heating</li><li>Small Development of only four detached houses</li><li>Off-Street Parking</li><li>Double Glazed Windows</li><li>A short walk to Rathgar, Rathmines, Ranelagh and Terenure villages</li><li>Tucked away behind security gates</ul>"
      },
